[2026-09-26 17:17:53] [claude-sdk] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfRinj4aLUiSYwhUNHvtH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"P7 is finished, which completes the whole plan (P0–P7). Everything is committed and pushed to `at22/session-waiting` (latest commit `c407362`); nothing is merged into main yet. The only thing left out was moving Codex to its app-server; Codex still runs through `codex exec`, which works.\n\n**What P7 added**\n- **Racing:** the \"create workspace\" screen now has \"競走させる\" checkboxes for other agents. Each checked agent gets its own worktree from the same starting commit and the same instruction, named `<name>-claude`, `<name>-grok` and so on. You compare them in the review tab. Right-click the winner → \"この案を採る…\" shows the losers with their uncommitted-change counts, and deletes them only after you confirm.\n- **Dispatch from the orchestrator:** the orchestrator writes a gate file with `dispatch: grok` (plus optional `name:` and `base:`).\n  - Nothing happens until you click 許可 on the gate panel. AT22 then creates the worktree, starts that agent in it, and when the agent's first turn ends writes `<id>.result` next to the gate file: status, workspace, branch, session, and the agent's reply.\n  - If the worktree or the agent can't be created or started, it writes `status: failed` with the reason, so the orchestrator isn't left waiting.\n  - The format is in `docs/orchestrator-gate.md`.\n\n**Layout bug I found and fixed on the way:** at the default 1100pt width, the left mode rail was pushed mostly off the window. The workspace pane (P3) and the fourth \"d レビュー\" tab (P5) had made the right side too wide. Now:\n- the tabs drop their romaji labels when space is short;\n- the window's minimum width grows with the open panes (about 950pt with both open), so the gate panel still fits.\n\nI also fixed a crash in the screenshot mode that came from the Dock badge code.\n\n**Checks run:**\n- `swift build` succeeds and the self-check ends with `p0: ok`. The new self-checks cover gate parsing, racing and choosing a winner against real git, and dispatch writing a failure result.\n- Dispatch end to end with a fake agent: 13/13 pass. With real Grok: 12/12 pass, and the result file contained `status: done` and `PONG`.\n- I looked at renders at 950 and 1100 wide; nothing overlaps and the rail stays visible.\n\n**Things for you:**\n- This session isn't allowed to run git in your main checkout, so I couldn't re-check that the patch still applies there (it did as of P6). To check or apply it: `git diff 9ae99e9 origin/at22/session-waiting | git apply --check` from `/Users/konnotakuto/Swift_PRJS/AT22_Glass_Cockpit`.\n- A test transcript from earlier (`57785b47-….jsonl`) is still in `~/.claude/projects`. Deleting it was blocked for me, so please remove it by hand.\n- If you use Hermes with Anthropic models, it may borrow Claude Code's login, which Anthropic's terms forbid. Your current setup (xAI OAuth) isn't affected.\n- Several MCP connectors (Microsoft 365, Asana, Atlassian, ClickUp, Linear, Monday) need authorising in your connector settings, and originkit failed to connect. None of them were needed here.\n\nresult: AT22 P7 is done and pushed to `at22/session-waiting` (c407362): racing several agents from one commit, dispatch from the orchestrator gate with results written back, and a fix for the rail being pushed off-screen; self-check and fake-agent and real-Grok end-to-end runs all pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":215899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":396},"output_tokens":701,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_